From 830a3f8e54314d7969a9539b10e87bd871dc9c3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: will <wrouesnel@wrouesnel.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:23:18 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] manager: Add RemoteLoginTakeover to hand local sessions
 to remote logins

With daemon/RemoteLoginTakeover=true, a user authenticating at a remote login
screen may take over their existing session on a local seat: the seat is
switched to a login screen, and once the session is inactive it is unlocked and
exposed through the RemoteDisplay interface (on its GdmLocalDisplay) with the
remote client's id, so gnome-remote-desktop hands the client over to it.
Logging in again locally takes the session back as usual.

Also make switch_to_compatible_user_session() refuse to activate or unlock a
session that is incompatible with the caller (e.g. a local seat session on
behalf of a remote login screen).
---
